# Trading Glossary

## Swing

A confirmed turning point in price.

---

## Market Structure

The sequence of highs and lows that describes market behavior.

---

## BOS (Break of Structure)

A continuation signal indicating the prevailing market structure remains intact.

---

## CHOCH (Change of Character)

A potential reversal signal where the existing market structure changes direction.

---

## Trend

The current directional bias derived from market structure.

---

## Structural Level

A support or resistance level derived from confirmed swing points.

---

## Structural Strength

A score representing the reliability of a structural level.

---

## Liquidity

Areas where stop-loss orders or resting orders are likely concentrated.

---

## Supply Zone

An area where selling pressure is expected.

---

## Demand Zone

An area where buying pressure is expected.

---

## Order Block

The final opposing candle before a strong impulsive move.

---

## Fair Value Gap (FVG)

A price imbalance created by rapid market movement.

---

## Premium

Price trading above equilibrium.

---

## Discount

Price trading below equilibrium.